{"title":"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems\">2003 AMC 12A #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems\">2003 AMC 10A #25</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit number, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the quotient and the remainder, respectively, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. For how many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31a6cd957da325a37d10bbf4c8078775c574306d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6ae018908e77ecc25b6ea19a260d82365a0fe5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 8180\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 8181\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 8182\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 9000\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 9090$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit number is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits become the quotient, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits become the remainder, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can be any integer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be any integer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive. \n</p><p>For each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaed782d24999db75d0f9c1135c53df2692d99ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot10\\cdot10=900$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e060b19f919ceeb7dc0093a9199fa9df6ab5a046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{100}{11} \\right\\rfloor = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"45\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce04a7d147d142fb4def4f61f8c4596eb67e1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r \\equiv 0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Since there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> \"extra\" possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc20bccf186adffa7225f53d842ad2a27c63266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/0597aea89941058d9acf9bf570b94bf66ec2a4b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{900}{11} \\right\\rfloor = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc20bccf186adffa7225f53d842ad2a27c63266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce04a7d147d142fb4def4f61f8c4596eb67e1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r \\equiv 0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, the number of possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce04a7d147d142fb4def4f61f8c4596eb67e1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r \\equiv 0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a942b7ae2e436560956335561fafcb6027a39b6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900\\cdot9+81\\cdot1=8181 \\Rightarrow\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"243\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b0643329458b2e2a3b374bf5ec7a6671d912fc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r\\equiv0\\pmod{11}\\Rightarrow100q+r\\equiv0\\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"18\" />. This means that any number whose quotient and remainder sum is divisible by 11 must also be divisible by 11. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad2052ae97b7ca1559e80b981d67232fd2f6590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{99990-10010}{11}+1=8181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"38\" /> possible values. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a6a985938157c3ac74eb9ebcecd26518fad15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }8181}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/18396b1d04475fed55fd7c1b75cd4d85133210be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> be the five digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5050b5d0f0b56e5aa00079f614bc21ba672d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/247f6c0d737a321109a2d277133be6dad904ff43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = de$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. By the divisibility rules of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1969567f071b08585c3097680bb818fbfa3bf77e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = a - b + c \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3e359713680d4954a3218063bd9cb92767e167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = -d + e \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af4e78ddc74587858d0e20246529086b9d06e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q + r = a - b + c - d + e = abcde = n \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisble by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af6d6fcc0af356e07310226cede1ef944c0b20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{99990 - 10010}{11} + 1 = 8181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"38\" /> five-digit multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a6a985938157c3ac74eb9ebcecd26518fad15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }8181}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OpGHj-B0_hg?t=672\">https://youtu.be/OpGHj-B0_hg?t=672</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\